*********************** DFS **********************************

 * DFS is a traversal technique which involves the idea of recursion and backtracking.
 * DFS goes in-depth, i.e., traverses all nodes by going ahead,
 * and when there are no further nodes to traverse in the current path,
 * then it backtracks on the same path and traverses other unvisited nodes.
 *
 * Imagine navigating through a maze where you follow one path as deep as it goes,
 * and when you can’t proceed further, you backtrack to the last junction and try a different route.
 *
 *
 * Start from a chosen node and mark it as visited, storing it in the traversal list.
 * Look at all the neighbors of the current node using the adjacency list.
 * For each neighbor, if it is not visited, recursively apply DFS on that neighbor.
 * This process continues, going deeper into one path until no unvisited nodes remain.
 * Once a path is fully explored, backtrack to explore the remaining neighbors.
 * Repeat until all nodes in the graph have been visited.